			<div class="content" id="post-content-4834196">
									

<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">[+]&nbsp;Overall</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">[-]&nbsp;Overall</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>My biggest issue with this is that a lot of the writing is not good: I'd really advise running this through an automated checker like e.g. libreoffice writer so you can catch easy to find mistakes like the lack of capitalisation etc. I've tried to highlight as much as I can here but I have almost certainly missed stuff cos there's just&#8230;a lot.</p>
<p>Beyond this, the jump between the exploration logs and the interview is too big: there's no connective writing between them so it just feels&#8230;too sudden? Like in part because -2 doesn't show up in the explorations at all and in part because thre's not really like, any reference to the events of the explorations in it or anything so it's just&#8230;there?</p>
<p>The actual exploration logs are fine but they feel&#8230;a little directionless? I don't think this is necessarily an issue so much as the slight lack of focus on the interesting events: two people being grabbed by a snake feels like it should be a huge focal event, rather than something which kinda happens in the background, y'know?</p>
<p>It also kinda feels like a lot of this is building up without a clear direction: that might be easier to introduce once you've written more of it, it's hard to tell; but it doesn't feel like all the elements are going to come together in some kind of satisfying conclusion yet.</p>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">[-]&nbsp;Overall</a></div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">[+]&nbsp;Line&nbsp;By&nbsp;Line</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">[-]&nbsp;Line&nbsp;By&nbsp;Line</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p><em>Gonna note that I can miss stuff; flag things which are right as being wrong and indeed flag things which are deliberately wrong.</em><br />
<em>I'll likely use <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">strikethrough</span> to indicate stuff to remove and <span style="color: green">green text</span> to indicate stuff to add.</em></p>
<blockquote>
<p>The abandoned Mining factory in ██████ ███████, Mongolia</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I'd probably name this place: anyone with clearance to see this file almost certainly has clearance to see where it is; otherwise how would they know where to go.</p>
<p>Also this image is ~4MB in size and pretty tiny in the page: I'd recommend opening it in an image editing program and downscaling it (you can ask in #site11 on IRC if you're having difficulty with this)</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Item #: SCP-XXXX</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I wouldn't necessarily bother including the Item # and Object Class lines at the start if you're using a header that includes them too.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Containment Area M21 is <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">to be</span> located <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">in</span> 300m <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">deep</span> underground <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">of</span><span style="color: green">in</span> the Gobi desert in Mongolia.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I would probably specify that SCP-XXXX-2 is to be stored in this containment area, or at least tie it into the SCP file more.</p>
<p>The 'to be' is technically fine but generally it's advised to say what the Containment Procedures are, rather than should be. 'deep' is to be cut because we can assume that &quot;300m underground&quot; means &quot;down&quot; and it feels clunky here.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-XXXX-2 is to be held in a 5&#160;m cube made of entirely Tungsten metal, the walls are to be (50m) thick on each side, with no gap for <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">planetary or</span> organic life to enter.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>My concern with this is that it's a lot of detail that doesn't feel important: the exact size and thickness of the cube aren't really that important; and neither is the exact material it's made of; particularly since none of this detail is referenced later.</p>
<p>Something like:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-XXXX-2 is held in a tungsten cube that cannot be accessed.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Would be clearer and conciser.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The air ventilation of the cell will be 3000 miles (4828.032 kilometers) in length away from the cell and to be checked three times a week.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The foundation always uses metric (so no miles figure) and I would not specify the length to that precision, or indeed, any precision generally? Also like&#8230;3000 miles is really far: like, for reference, Tokyo is 1877 miles from Ulaanbaatar and Manila is 2434 miles from Ulaanbaatar.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>If any <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">of</span> humanoids that reside<span style="text-decoration: line-through;">s</span> in SCP-XXXX-1 <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">are to</span> move from their respective station</p>
</blockquote>
<p>'humanoids' feels odd here: I believe the people you are referring to are actually humans? 'respective station' is odd: generally in english, station refers to either 'position in society' or like 'a train station', so 'position' would be better than 'respective station'.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>they are to be immediately apprehended and held in the same containment cell as SCP-XXXX and <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">is</span> questioned for further notice.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Do you mean SCP-XXXX-2 here? Also 'questioned for further notice' doesn't make sense; I'd likely used 'interrogated' in place of 'questioned' and I'd probably cut the 'for further notice' completely.</p>
<p>I'd also strongly suggest putting them in a separate containment chamber; and reordering so it's &quot;immediately apprehended and interrogated before being held in the&#8230;&quot;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>No more than five personnel<span style="color: green">, wearing</span> <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">in</span> Hazmat suit<span style="color: green">s,</span> are to enter SCP-XXXX-1 <span style="color: green">at the same time time</span>.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Specifying 'at the same time' prevents the implication that only five people can ever enter.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>and no unauthorized personnel and civilian are to be in the proximity of the area or enter SCP-XXXX-1</p>
</blockquote>
<p>this can be assumed: they are unauthorized so they are not allowed in.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Unauthorized personnel under level 5 entering the area without permission are given Class C amnestic and is reassigned to a different project. Civilian is to given Class-A amnestic, and is to quarantined based on the severity of their bodily form and psyche.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I'd cut this; we don't need to know how they're punished and we can assume folk who access without permission are to be punished.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>In the event of <span style="color: green">a</span> Containment Breach</p>
</blockquote>
<p>&quot;Containment Breach&quot; doesn't need to be capitalised here.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>all on sight researchers</p>
</blockquote>
<p>'site': 'sight' is 'vision'</p>
<blockquote>
<p>or <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">to</span> stay in shelter until <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">the</span> MTF Theta-4 (<span style="color: green">&quot;</span>Gardeners<span style="color: green">&quot;</span>) <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">are to</span> arrive at the facility and apprehend<span style="text-decoration: line-through;">ed</span> the entity.</p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-CXXX consists of two components; a cave (SCP-XXXX-1) and <span style="color: green">a</span> humanoid protecting it (SCP-XXXX-2).</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I would generally avoid defining SCP-XXXX in this way because it forces you to refer to -1 and -2 a lot and means you almost never refer to the whole. In this case, I'd likely define -2 as the base anomaly and leave the cave as -1.</p>
<p>The semi-colon (;) should be a colon here (:) too technically but I think the first change means you don't need to worry about this.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-XXXX-2 resembles a small Hun human male in his mid-teens, standing 169&#160;cm (5,5) and weight around 55&#160;kg (123 lbs).</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Again, foundation only uses metric so don't include the imperial conversions here. This said: his exact height and weight aren't important for a reader to understand the anomaly so I'd probably just cut this. I'd also avoid using 'resembles' and other vague words: just say he is a human here even if he's a human with anomalous properties.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Back hair and brown eyes.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This is a sentence fragment (i.e, the issue is it contains no verb: something like &quot;SCP-XXXX-2 has black hair and brown eyes&quot; would be clearer, though if you do cut the height/weight in the last sentence, you could refer to these at the end of the sentence. I'm also assuming 'Back hair' was a typo for 'Black hair'.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Footnote 1: A deel (Mongolian: дээл [deːɮ]; Buryat: дэгэл, [dɛɡɛɮ]) is an item of traditional clothing commonly worn since centuries ago among the Mongols and other nomadic tribes of Central Asia, including various Turkic peoples, and can be made from cotton, silk, wool, or brocade</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This isn't a very good description of what a deel is because it entirely focuses on who wears it and what it's made from; whereas if you're putting a footnote in to explain what it is, you want to focus on 'what does it look like'.</p>
<p>It also looks like it's ripped from wikipedia: this is fine but you will have to cite it if so. I recommend checking out the <a href="/image-use-policy">Image Use Policy</a> here since it talks a lot about how to ensure material is compatible with the wiki's license and how to attribute the images; whilst wikipedia words aren't an image, the same policy applies here.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>which <span style="color: green">has</span> been ripped and <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">throne</span><span style="color: green">torn</span>, however, SCP-XXXX-2 refuse<span style="text-decoration: line-through;">d</span>##greens## to change it.</p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p>Instance of SCP-XXXX-2 anomalies properties, are manifestation of Reptilian (Saurosida) entity strongly resembling a dragon made out of natural components.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The start of this is kinda a mess; I'd probably suggest rephrasing to e.g.:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-XXXX-2 has the ability to manifest entities made out of natural components which resemble a dragon</p>
</blockquote>
<p>That said: &quot;natural components&quot; is super vague; and it might be worth specifying if this is Chinese style dragons or Western style dragons</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Its full length is impossible to measure but is hypothesized to be between 1000 and 2000 kilometers.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>&quot;Its&quot; is unclear if you mean &quot;SCP-XXXX-2&quot; or &quot;the entity&quot;; I'd probably use 'unknown' in place of 'impossible to measure' because it seems to me that it'd be easy to measure this theoretically if it stood still. I'd also use 'estimated' in place of 'hypothesized' here.</p>
<p>1000 and 2000 kilometers is also too big. Like&#8230;godzilla is maybe 300m tall at most (it varies depending on the film; usually 100m is closer to the average), which means this thing is 5000 godzillas long at minimum and likely 15000 godzilla's long using the average godzilla height)</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-XXXX-1 is a Cognitohazardous cave under a destroyed and abandoned Mining factory</p>
</blockquote>
<p>neither cognitohazardous nor mining should be capitalised here. I would probably only use one of 'destroyed' and 'abandoned' here since there's a lot of overlap in their meaning. Also 'cognitohazardous' is super broad and you really do have to specify how here; or just&#8230;not mention the properties at all.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>it is measured to be around 4000 kilometers deep</p>
</blockquote>
<p>4000km deep takes you through the crust of the earth (30km thick) and the mantle of the earth (2900&#160;km thick) and into the outer core of the planet.</p>
<p>The deepest mine in the world, currently, is the Mponeng gold mine. It extends about 4km deep, or around 1/1000th of the depth of this mine.</p>
<p>Like I get this is like&#8230;anomalous and stuff but it does not feasible for the mine to be this deep without this being a lot more of a big deal than it currently is.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>However, how big SCP-XXXX-omega mass is impossible to measure.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>what is SCP-XXXX-omega? This is one of the only two places here you mention it and you never define it.</p>
<p>The other place implies they can enter SCP-XXXX-omega which makes measuring it's mass feel weird? So I'd probably cut this but??</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-XXXX-1 resides a snake-like creature approximately 200 kilometers, maybe even bigger.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>'maybe even bigger' is real casual and I would not include it. Rephrasing to lead with the snake creature would be clearer e.g.: &quot;A snake-like creature approximately 200km long resides in SCP-XXXX&quot;. Again though, 200km is <em>really</em> big to the point where if you said 2km, I would say it's probably too big still.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>About fifty kilometers down<span style="color: green">, there is</span> a massive field stretching further from the human eye</p>
</blockquote>
<p>'stretching further than the human eye can see' is a good metaphor to grasp for but this is a SCP description: you want to describe things objectively using set sizes rather than vague things like 'larger than can be seen'</p>
<blockquote>
<p>filled with stationary humanoids varies in ages, they're made out of natural components, different species of flowers but growing in the same root</p>
</blockquote>
<p>this feels&#8230;muddled. It probably needs to be a few sentences to make it read right but I'm not exactly sure how best to do that.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Picture of a wooden horse taken during the second exploration</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I'd probably move this into the second exploration</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The instants of SCP-XXXX-1's anomalous properties became apparent when entering the area.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I'm not sure what you mean by 'instants' here but it feels like this would be better as 'SCP-XXXX-1's anomalous properties become&#8230;'</p>
<p>Then again, 'anomalous properties' is the kinda super vague statement I'd generally urge folk to avoid cos it can be basically anything; it'd be more effective to say something like &quot;Radio signals cut off inside SCP-XXXX-1&quot; say.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>It is hypnotized that SCP-XXXX-1 refracts of all organic structures, even humans and animals, but it is yet to be backed up.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>'hypnotized' should be 'hypothesized'. I'm not sure what you're getting at with 'refracts': maybe like, 'restructures all organic structures' or 'reshapes' or something? 'refracts' is a phenomenon where light changes direction when it enters a partially transparent material and unlikely to be what you're looking for here.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-XXXX was discovered by serious of civilian interviews and gossips in ███████ ████████ after the mass destruction of major mining facilities.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>'SCP-XXXX was discovered during the investigation of the destruction of mining facilities in [place name].'</p>
<p>As before, redacting the place name here is a bad idea and you should just name a place here.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>It is noted that <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">the</span> SCP-XXXX-2 was already known among<span style="color: green">st</span> the locals as a fairy tale hero, with SCP-XXXX-1 mentioned multiple times during the interviews indicating they<span style="text-decoration: line-through;">'re</span> might be connected in some way.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>'fairy tale hero' feels super casual here; maybe make mention of it appearing in local mythology instead? Also it feels like this needs to setup a firmer connection spatially between the mine and -1 (as in, where is -1 in relation to the mine?) and a firmer connection between -2 and -1.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The investigation into <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">the origins of</span> SCP-XXXX-1 and its relation with SCP-XXXX-2 is ongoing.</p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p>Due to the unknown nature of SCP-XXXX-1, MTF-Zeta-9 (Mole Rats) were <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">send</span><span style="color: green">sent</span> in to explore the cave and return with the sample.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>'deployed' would be more clinical than 'sent in'; and 'return with the sample' needs additional detail to indicate what kinda samples they're looking for: at the moment it's just&#8230;kinda vague.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>However they did not return in time, and Recovery team was dispatched to collect the remaining of the team.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This feels like it should be after the first exploration log; rather than spoiling that they don't return immediately before like&#8230;getting to the log, y'know? Same goes for the rest of this paragraph.</p>
<p>Something like &quot;After they had not returned 8 hours later, a recovery team was dispatched to investigate&quot; would flow better; with the option of increasing 8 hours or decreasing it depending on how you feel.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>They found MTF-Zeta-9 (Mole Rats) team's all none organic materials like guns, vest, and food cans some completely full and other empty.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Something like &quot;Only the non-organic components of MTF Zeta-9's equipment were found.&quot; would be clearer; you don't need to specify the mole rats every time just, y'know, to cut down the length.</p>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>Date:</strong> █/██20██</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I wouldn't redact this either; knowing when this happened is important contextualisation for how long the events took to play out etc.</p>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>Subject:</strong> inside of SCP-XXXX-1</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I'd cut this; there's not really a subject so you don't need to say this.</p>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>Team Members:</strong> Agent<span style="color: green">s</span> Luna, Ouyulan, Zachary, and Sunder.</p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>Agent Olson:</strong> Command<span style="color: green">,</span> we are entering SCP-XXXX-omega.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>same comment about -omega not being defined as earlier; I think you're wanting -1 here?</p>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>Command:</strong> Roger that! stay in touch as long as you can!</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I'd avoid using ! as much as possible: the more you use it, the less emphasis it carries. Also it's the end of a sentence, so the 'stay' after the first should be capitalised.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>the five agents began to hike down the cave, the light started to dim away.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Capitalised start of sentences, even here.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>you and Agent Sunder grew up <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">closer</span><span style="color: green">close to</span> here, right?</p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p>Yup the real countryside pumpkin is me.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>do you mean 'bumpkin' here? 'country' would read better than 'countryside' too</p>
<p>not sure what you're trying to imply by 'mouth by mouth forum'; perhaps 'it was spread via word of mouth'?</p>
<blockquote>
<p><span style="text-decoration: line-through;">Quite</span><span style="color: green">Quiet</span>, any of you hear<span style="text-decoration: line-through;">d</span> anything?</p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p>the ground started to shake and small rubble falls on top of Agent Zachary's head! Olson looked up, there was long intervened vines and roots seemingly identical to a snake skeleton.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>'rubble' is collective; I think you want like 'a small rock' here? 'intervened' is probably meant to be 'intertwined' or 'tangled'?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>TIME: Corrupted</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Ending on the time feels kinda janky here; like&#8230;why would it be presented here and not earlier? or like, throughout this since this log takes place over an hour or so</p>
<blockquote>
<p>At least we have natural light! I reckon the snake attacked us because of our light.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>why are none of them questioning why there is natural light deep within a mine</p>
<blockquote>
<p>or does the air is less timid than when we eventually hiked down</p>
</blockquote>
<p>'or is the air less timid than when we started' would be clearer though&#8230;timid is not the word you're looking for here. I'm not sure what the right word is though.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Agent Olson gets up and looks around and breathing in and out slowly.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I'd replace the second and with a comma</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The camera pans out to a giant field filled with what seems to be an ecosystem.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>&#8230;how does the camera pan out? Why did no-one notice it before since this is implied to be right there since it's just&#8230;the camera showing it?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>than the animal above</p>
</blockquote>
<p>'than animals above ground'</p>
<blockquote>
<p>There are very big threes</p>
</blockquote>
<p>trees?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The light source of this… the place is completely natural, I have no idea where the sun is even shining from the top of us.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>How do they know the light source is natural? It seems like they have no idea where the light is coming from here</p>
<blockquote>
<p>But the air becoming even timider than the last cave we were in.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>&#8230;do you mean 'thinner'?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>His cough becomes more severe as he goes.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>'as he goes' is missing like a 'towards the light' kinda thing where it says where he's going, y'know?</p>
<p>Also this is bolded instead of italicised</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Suddenly Olson turned back and saw a hill fill with flowers, he didn't see before</p>
</blockquote>
<p>These should be impartial records of what happened: words like 'Suddenly' feel really out of place here; and 'he didn't see before' should be conveyed via what he says rather than the transcript assuming it.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>oh fuck, maybe that place is forcing my allergies to kick me in the balls.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This feels weird like the implication is the hill is far away and unlikely to be the source of the coughing? It seems pollen from the nearby plants would be a much more believable explanation here</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Once they were at the top of the hill, the camera zoom to an enormous Yurt, behind the Yurt what seemed to be humanoids, stationary.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I again would not refer to the camera doing stuff; generally an MTF will want to keep hands free so this is more&#8230;passive body camera recording than active filming, y'know?</p>
<p>Yurt also should not be capitalised here; and this should probably be a few sentences where they like, explicitly walk around the yurt a little or something so they can see the humanoids</p>
<blockquote>
<p>But this one… seems incredible (coughs) a saturated.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I'm not sure what you're trying to get at with 'a saturated' here</p>
<blockquote>
<p>they<span style="color: green">'re</span> all people!</p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p>on a bee made out of natural components sitting on a yellow flower</p>
</blockquote>
<p>this phrasing implies there's something special about a bee being made of natural components but bees are y'know, already made of natural components</p>
<blockquote>
<p>And yet… this thing <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">had</span><span style="color: green">has</span> already taken a life.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Why 'a' life? Like, there's four members of his team who have disappeared so far; and like there's room for him to be uncertain about some of them but only in two people pairs so he has to think either 0, 2 or 4 of them are dead</p>
<blockquote>
<p>But I want to ask you <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">serious</span><span style="color: green">a series</span> of questions.</p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p>Its alright, but we have estimated that your age is about 2000 years.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>What led them to this estimate?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>It was <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">quite</span><span style="color: green">quiet</span> for three minutes.</p>
</blockquote>
</div>
